{
  "dom_id": "step-q136921",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ above. If the normal equation corresponding to the system $Ax=b$ is given below, what is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 20 \\\\ 20 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+40+4=54.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
